
VERSION 2 — PROPOSED UNIFIED ACADEMY SCOPE
Working proposal | 19 November 2026 | Miss Jess's leadership items approved; developer feasibility and deployment verification pending

1. Purpose and positioning
Platform name: Koruna Academy.
Objective: Extend the existing Academy to serve KA and KC through one platform, reducing duplicated development, hosting, administration, and maintenance where technically feasible.
Baseline: All original feature descriptions above remain unchanged. They describe source-code functionality, not necessarily verified production capability.

2. Proposed content structure
KA Training — KA-specific courses and learning paths.
KC Training — KC-specific courses, including AI tools and Hybrid AI-Enabled EA/VA training.
Shared Training — common courses available to both organisations, maintained once rather than duplicated.
The three categories are a proposed logical content structure. Developers must confirm whether native folders, categories, learning paths, or another supported mechanism is best.

3. Proposed access model
KA employees — KA Training and Shared Training only.
KC employees — KC Training and Shared Training only.
KA trainers/team leaders — KA and relevant shared content and records within their authorised scope.
KC trainers/team leaders — KC and relevant shared content and records within their authorised scope.
Super Admins — cross-organisation access for authorised central administration.
Course visibility, assignments, enrolment, reporting, assessments, progress, certificates, and downloadable resources must respect organisation and role permissions. Enforcement must be server-side, not merely hidden navigation.
Shared courses may be reused across organisations, but learner records and organisation-specific reporting must remain distinguishable.

